    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Concating by axis=1 means that both responses are kept together. This means that when we split the data into training vs. validation data, both responses (and the prompt) both into the same set. With axis=0, the responses for the same prompt could be split between the training and validation sets which would be cheating.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will only train on responses which did not have a tie. A key assumption with our approach is that there should be nothing special about ties. Since we will pass each response separately through the model, we can detect ties simply by cases where the model labels both response a 1 (or 0).\n",
        "\n",
        "Obviously, excluding ties from our training set reduces the size of our training set. We could include those results by including both responses. The question would be whether to have the labels both be 0 or 1 or something else. Definitely something to try but let's get a baseline first.\n",
        "\n",
        "Make sure to still have the ties in the validation set.\n",
        "\n",
        "Filter out the ties from the training/validation sets after the split - that way adding them in later is much easier.\n",
        "\n",
        "Resetting the index will allow us to quickly reconnect the responses for a given prompt."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7ma2QO_Y0Quw"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "df2 = pd.concat([df,df_a,df_b],axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "raw_train, raw_validation = train_test_split(df2, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "raw_train = raw_train.reset_index()\n",
        "raw_validation = raw_validation.reset_index()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0MoOhRG1az8C"
      },
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def setup(df):\n",
        "\n",
        "  m1 = df[\"winner_tie\"] == 0\n",
        "\n",
        "  m2 = df2[\"encode_fail_a\"] == False\n",
        "  m3 = df2[\"encode_fail_b\"] == False\n",
        "\n",
        "  temp1 = df.loc[m1&m2,[\"index\",\"text_a\",\"winner_model_a\"]]\n",
        "  temp2 = df.loc[m1&m3,[\"index\",\"text_b\",\"winner_model_b\"]]\n",
        "\n",
        "  temp1 = temp1.rename(columns={\"text_a\":\"text\",\"winner_model_a\":\"winner_model\"})\n",
        "  temp2 = temp2.rename(columns={\"text_b\":\"text\",\"winner_model_b\":\"winner_model\"})\n",
        "\n",
        "  temp1[\"response\"] = \"a\"\n",
        "  temp2[\"response\"] = \"b\"\n",
        "\n",
        "  return pd.concat([temp1,temp2])\n",
        "\n",
        "train_df = setup(raw_train)\n",
        "validate_df = setup(raw_validation)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MPjzpiyZiJha"
      },
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
