              "summary": "{\n  \"name\": \"val_df\",\n  \"rows\": 15764,\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"column\": \"index\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 16605,\n        \"min\": 7,\n        \"max\": 57474,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 14185,\n        \"samples\": [\n          54833,\n          10326,\n          53730\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"text\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 15726,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"A murderer is condemned to death. He has to choose between three rooms. The first is full of raging fires, the second is full of assassins with loaded guns, and the third is full of lions that haven't eaten in 3 years. Which room is safest for him? Lay out your complete thought process. - It is difficult to determine which room would be the safest for the murderer, as it ultimately depends on the specific circumstances and individual preferences of the murderer.\\n\\nHowever, we can analyze each potential room and its potential risks:\\n\\n1. The first room with raging fires: This room would clearly be the safest option if the murderer values his own life above all else. The intense heat and flames would likely make it impossible for the murderer to survive for long in such a room.\\n2. The second room with assassins: This room would be very dangerous for the murderer, as he would be at risk of being killed by the assassins. Even if he were able to avoid being killed, he would likely be terrified of the assassins and their loaded guns.\\n3. The third room with lions: This room would also be extremely dangerous for the murderer, as the lions have not eaten in 3 years and may be starving. The lions could potentially attack the murderer, and the knowledge that they have not eaten in so long could likely cause the murderer significant fear and anxiety.\\n\\nIn conclusion, while it is impossible to say for certain which room would be the safest, it appears that the first room with raging fires would likely be the safest option if the murderer values his own life above all else. However, this ultimately depends on the specific circumstances and individual preferences of the murderer. 1\",\n          \"Can you explain the attention mechanism in transformer models? How are the values of K, Q, and V determined? I understand that the purpose is to make words appear more or less important to the model, but how do the K, Q, and V values do that? - Here is an explanation of the attention mechanism in Transformer models:\\n\\n- K, Q, and V stand for keys, queries, and values. They are learned representations of the input sequence.\\n\\n- For each word in the sequence, the model computes a \\\"query\\\" vector Q and a \\\"key\\\" vector K. \\n\\n- The key vectors K are computed from the entire input sequence. So each word has a learned \\\"key\\\" representation.\\n\\n- The query vector Q for a particular word is computed based on just that single word. \\n\\n- To calculate attention, the query Q of the first word is \\\"dot producted\\\" with all the key vectors K. This gives attention scores for how relevant each other word is to the first word.\\n\\n- The values V are also learned representations of the input sequence, computed similarly to the keys. \\n\\n- A softmax function is applied to the attention scores to convert them to weights that sum to 1. \\n\\n- The output is computed as a weighted sum of the value vectors V, using the attention weights. This selects a context vector that represents the most relevant parts of the input sequence for that word.\\n\\nSo in summary, the keys K determine what aspects of other words are relevant for attention, the queries Q pick out the relevance to the target word, and the values V provide the actual context information that gets combined based on the attention weights. This allows the model to focus on the most important parts of the sequence for understanding each word. 1\",\n          \"What can I expect from this light novel? And what are the good things about it and pitfalls? Don't include major spoilers.\\n```\\nTitle: \\u9053\\u679c\\u3066\\u306e\\u5411\\u3053\\u3046\\u306e\\u5149\\nDescription: \\\"Just what kind of pretense is that. Is this some new form of torment?\\u201d\\n\\nYuna, a plain village girl, suddenly lost her plain day to day life. After being requested to by a mysterious light in a bright white world, Yuna finds herself in the body of a beautiful saint. However, what awaited her there was; the contemptuous gaze of the saint\\u2019s fiance, First Holy Knight Asyut; the cold detachment from her attendants; and the tense atmosphere of the entire palace. Yuna, alone in her crippling confusion, still tries to fulfill her duty as the saint\\u2019s substitute, until one night when she discovers the saint\\u2019s sins beyond the spiral staircase\\u2026?!\\\"\\n\\nJapanese description: \\\"\\u6b8b\\u9177\\u306a\\u5947\\u8de1\\u306b\\u3001\\u79c1\\u306f\\u306a\\u306b\\u3092\\u306e\\u3053\\u305b\\u308b\\u3060\\u308d\\u3046\\u3002\\n\\u5e73\\u51e1\\u306a\\u753a\\u5a18\\u3060\\u3063\\u305f\\u30e6\\u30fc\\u30ca\\u306e\\u65e5\\u5e38\\u306f\\u5510\\u7a81\\u306b\\u5931\\u308f\\u308c\\u305f\\u3002\\u771f\\u3063\\u767d\\u3044\\u7a7a\\u9593\\u3067\\u51fa\\u4f1a\\u3063\\u305f\\u6b63\\u4f53\\u4e0d\\u660e\\u306e\\u300c\\u5149\\u300d\\u306b\\u8acb\\u308f\\u308c\\u308b\\u304c\\u307e\\u307e\\u3001\\u300c\\u8056\\u5973\\u300d\\u306e\\u8eab\\u4f53\\u306b\\u5165\\u3063\\u3066\\u751f\\u6d3b\\u3059\\u308b\\u3053\\u3068\\u306b\\u306a\\u3063\\u3066\\u3057\\u307e\\u3063\\u305f\\u30e6\\u30fc\\u30ca\\u3092\\u5f85\\u3063\\u3066\\u3044\\u305f\\u3082\\u306e\\u306f\\u3001\\u300c\\u8056\\u5973\\u300d\\u306e\\u5a5a\\u7d04\\u8005\\u3001\\u795e\\u8056\\u9a0e\\u58eb\\u30a2\\u30b7\\u30e5\\u30fc\\u30c8\\u306e\\u601d\\u3044\\u304c\\u3051\\u306a\\u3044\\u4fae\\u8511\\u306e\\u307e\\u306a\\u3056\\u3057\\u3068\\u3001\\u4f8d\\u5973\\u305f\\u3061\\u306e\\u52aa\\u3081\\u3066\\u7121\\u611f\\u52d5\\u306a\\u8868\\u60c5\\u3001\\u305d\\u3057\\u3066\\u3001\\u738b\\u5bae\\u3092\\u3064\\u3064\\u3080\\u5f35\\u308a\\u3064\\u3081\\u305f\\u7a7a\\u6c17\\u3067\\u3042\\u3063\\u305f\\u3002\\n\\u308f\\u3051\\u3082\\u308f\\u304b\\u3089\\u305a\\u6df7\\u4e71\\u306e\\u307e\\u307e\\u3001\\u305d\\u308c\\u3067\\u3082\\u306a\\u3093\\u3068\\u304b\\u3084\\u3063\\u3066\\u3044\\u3053\\u3046\\u3068\\u6c7a\\u610f\\u3059\\u308b\\u30e6\\u30fc\\u30ca\\u3067\\u3042\\u3063\\u305f\\u304c\\u3001\\u3042\\u308b\\u591c\\u3001\\u87ba\\u65cb\\u968e\\u6bb5\\u306e\\u5965\\u306b\\u6f5c\\u3080\\u300c\\u8056\\u5973\\u300d\\u306e\\u7f6a\\u3092\\u77e5\\u308a\\u2026\\u2026!?\\\"\\n\\nTags: Arranged Marriage Beautiful Female Lead Body Swap Bodyguards Caring Protagonist Cold Love Interests Determined Protagonist Engagement Fantasy World Female Protagonist Hiding True Identity Honest Protagonist Kind Love Interests Knights Love Triangles Magic Mysterious Past Mystery Solving Past Plays a Big Role Politics Religions Saints Selfless Protagonist Sentimental Protagonist Stubborn Protagonist Suicides Transmigration\\n```\\n\\nReviews:\\n```\\nHonestly, until halfway through volume 2, I found the MC to be so naive, annoying, and s*upid. Is she a good person? Undoubtedly. But does that make for an enjoyable read? Absolutely not. The MC has been reincarnated into the body of a saint, who form the looks of it was a very horrible person. What annoys me is her soft personality i.e. Stuttering every time she starts a sentence, repeatedly saying sorry to everyone, and asking permission for everything.\\n[Spoiler:\\nThere is this one incident that really had me bashing my head against the wall. So the previous owner of the body was horrible, as stated before. Throwing people in jail and having them tortured for very petty reasons. But the new MC has taken it onto herself to rectify this and make it better, which I admit is a very admirable attitude. HOWEVER, what I do not agree with is her helping them personally. Mainly because the cause of their suffering and torment (aka her) appearing before them will not only freak the f*ck out of them, it will might even tempt them to take revenge. But NO, she, in her s*upid stubbornness, decides that she must help them. And when someone tries to kill her (she had his wife killed because he annoyed her), she stubbornly refuses to have him executed even though it would set a dangerous precedent and put her in more danger, and her naive reason is that \\\"there is a life st stake.\\\" !?!?!?!?!? Her naive and s*upidly simple optimistic outlook is displayed in her thought that \\\"she needed to get him to be positive somehow.\\\" Really? REALLY!? YOU KILL HIS WIFE AND YOU EXPECT HIM TO BE HAPPY DANDY ONCE HE IS RELEASED FROM JAIL!? WHAT KIND OF WEIRD MUSHROOM JUICE HAVE YOU BEEN DRINKING?!?!]\\n```\\n\\n```\\nI'd have probably given this a 5 stars if the MC wasn't so annoying. She's your typical gentle, caring and lovable main character. In fact she's so stereotypical that it feels like she has no personality. Every time something occurs, she gets away with it and forces her way through by simply stating \\\"Because I want to.\\\" Even when her surrounding tells her that it will cause huge trouble if she keeps insisting on the matter, giving her reasonable and fair arguments, she just doesn't seem to understand. She doesn't want anyone to die, she tries to take the blame on herself for the \\\"old\\\" Saint's mistakes, she is dense and doesn't notice others' feelings. She is so \\\"pure\\\" that it becomes really annoying, I like to read about a MC that uses her head, that uses reasoning and that is smart. I don't want to read a story that is about a typical Shojo Manga character. The side characters are way too indulging, almost as if they were waiting for her to make the move.\\nIf we have to talk about the world building, it's still a common \\\"Transported to another world and interacting with nobles\\\" setting. It has nothing new so to speak of. The story is not bad but the setting kind of throws it off.\\n```\\n\\n```\\nThis is a story about a young girl who dies and wakes up in someone else's body. The twist is, she only has one year to occupy that body before she dies again for real, and the original body was someone truly detestable and cruel. MC struggles to fit into her new role and not cause too much suspicion, but also does her best to live her one year without regrets and leave behind a better legacy for the original girl.\\nThe author really focuses on character development and it really shines in this novel. The MC's emotions feel genuine and she acts pretty much like you'd expect a bewildered young girl in a difficult situation to. That said, she still has that strong, kind, and stand-out MC quality so you want to root for her. The romance feels like it's gonna be sort of a reverse harem with a strong male lead; I'm really pumped to see how MC and Male lead's relationship develops further.\\nThe religious\\\\/political\\\\/social undertones also look promising, and the translator did a great job with this. I'm looking forward to reading the next chapters!\\n```\\n\\n```\\nPersonally, one of my favorite LNs and part of the reason is the MC. I've seen many people hating on her, but honestly, her personality is quite refreshing for me. Seeing so many shoujo LN heroines being selfish and so smart it's unrealistic, I like her, yes. She is really kind and caring, I love Yuna so much! Also, just because a character is a bit shy, likes helping others and is determined to do the right thing, doesn't mean that they don't have a personality.\\nAnyway, the other characters are also great and developed, like Asyut and Aeneas. They are given so much depth, I can't believe I found a LN this good. Same thing goes for the story.\\nI must say, kudos to Ilinox because her translations are superb and better than many others IMO. If she wasn't the one translating, I don't think this LN would be as good. Specially like how she doesn't include japanese honorifics, sorry for those who like it.\\n``` - The light novel \\\"\\u9053\\u679c\\u3066\\u306e\\u5411\\u3053\\u3046\\u306e\\u5149\\\" (The Light at the End of the Cruel Miracle) features a protagonist named Yuna who finds herself in the body of a saint with a terrible reputation. She must navigate the palace's political intrigues, the contempt of her fianc\\u00e9, and the cold treatment from her attendants. Despite these challenges, Yuna tries to fulfill her duty as the saint's substitute and uncover the truth about the saint's sins.\\n\\nThe novel has received mixed reviews. Some readers have praised the character development, particularly of the protagonist, while others have criticized her for being naive, annoying, and stubborn. The world building has also been a subject of debate, with some readers appreciating the detailed religious and political undertones, while others find it common and unoriginal.\\n\\nOne of the strengths of the novel is the focus on the protagonist's emotions and growth, which feel genuine and relatable. The romance aspect also has potential, with a possible reverse harem and a strong male lead. The translations have also been highly praised for their quality and attention to detail.\\n\\nHowever, some readers may find the protagonist's personality and behavior frustrating, as she can come across as overly kind, shy, and naive. The side characters have also been criticized for being one-dimensional and waiting for the protagonist to take action.\\n\\nOverall, \\\"\\u9053\\u679c\\u3066\\u306e\\u5411\\u3053\\u3046\\u306e\\u5149\\\" offers a unique take on the body swap genre, with a focus on character development and emotional growth. While some readers may find the protagonist and the world building to be clich\\u00e9d or unoriginal, others will appreciate the attention to detail and the quality of the translations. As with any novel, individual preferences will play a significant role in determining one's enjoyment of the story. 2\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"encode_fail\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"boolean\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 1,\n        \"samples\": [\n          false\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"label\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 1,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"tie\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 0,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 1,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
